  "slug": "sequences-promoter-38cf",
  "summary": "New evaluations show AlphaFold 3 accuracy dropping on novel RNAs while validation and scoring tools extend to nucleic acid complexes.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is evaluating and validating deep-learning predictions of RNA and protein-RNA structure against experimental references. An AlphaFold 3 assessment on over 1,300 protein-RNA complexes and about 270 RNA-only systems reports reduced fold and interface accuracy on novel RNAs. RPFace pairs a sequence-only interface predictor with a stratified benchmark intended to expose biased structural benchmarks. Validation and confidence tooling is also extended: conkit-validate is adapted to RNA as a mapless method, and ipSAE is generalized with directional PAE scoring to nucleic acid, ligand and ion interactions in AF3 and Boltz-2. Ribocentre-FoldBridge links chemical probing profiles to 3D models, and CryoID2 uses a 3D U-Net to identify protein and RNA in cryoEM maps. The emphasis is on generalization and reliability, not only on generating models.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-07"
}
